{"seq":12,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-none-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:35:50.337Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"9baa4626456a77878b1746f7f60ce6f14f31079cfa2aa20970f0f3cae096f04a","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, here's the Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL) and Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF) list for Kwame's account review. I read #coastal-team, #coastal-random, the Coastal Moss digests and your public Pellucid cutover note.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics** (Gulf Coast port drayage)\n- **#4419:** the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. It's listed as open in Moss's Coastal cheat sheet. See the conflict below.\n- **PD-8841:** chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. This is from your 8 Dec cutover note, and it says the screenshots are on the ticket. I found no status for it.\n- **No ticket number:** a CSV import bug on the Berth 2 yard map, from your cutover note. Moss's cheat sheet also names chassis pool validation at Gate 4 at shift change as the main friction point.\n- **No ticket number:** the terminal 4 drayage gate export for the 3 Nov handoff, from Moss's 2 Nov digest.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight** (Puget Sound barge operator)\n- **Feature request #882:** a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers (cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number:** the tide-table import macro failed on Terminal B. Engineering supplied a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher (cheat sheet).\n- **No ticket number:** DMF asked for a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift (Moss's 2 Nov digest).\n\n**Conflict on #4419:** the cheat sheet puts it on PHL (the report timeout). Moss's 2 Nov digest says Kwame's port account logged it for barge slip 7 schedule sync, next to the DMF request. I couldn't tell which is right, so it's under PHL above. Kwame should confirm before the review.\n\n**Left out:**\n- Pellow Home Living / Covey & Lark: PD-4821 and #8812.\n- Saltmarsh: PD-4824 and PD-4827.\n\nThe channels themselves had no PHL or DMF tickets, only the Pellow/PHL naming mix-up from 17 Feb. I can only see the channels you're in and public files, so anything in other channels or in private notes isn't covered."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
